["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>A deer is one hard trip. A moose is a weekend. Plan the pack out before you plan the shot.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Way out</th><th>Good for</th><th>Rules</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Your back</td><td>Anywhere</td><td>Edible portions</td></tr><tr><td>Sled</td><td>Snow, downhill</td><td>Edible portions</td></tr><tr><td>ATV (all terrain vehicle)</td><td>Where allowed</td><td>Wildlife Act, ORV Act, firearm transport</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Every edible portion comes out, however many trips <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the three ways out</summary><ul><li>Three ways out: on your back, on a sled, on the <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"ATV\">ATV</button> (all terrain vehicle).</li><li>The ATV has its own rulebook: the Wildlife Act, the Off Road Vehicle Act, and federal firearm transport rules.</li><li>The one rule that never changes: every edible portion comes out, however many trips it takes <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 490\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"490\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Where the meat is: quartering a deer</text>\n\n  <g stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\n    <!-- legs -->\n    <rect x=\"118\" y=\"196\" width=\"14\" height=\"70\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n    <rect x=\"140\" y=\"196\" width=\"14\" height=\"66\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n    <rect x=\"262\" y=\"196\" width=\"14\" height=\"70\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/>\n    <rect x=\"284\" y=\"196\" width=\"14\" height=\"66\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/>\n    <!-- body base -->\n    <ellipse cx=\"210\" cy=\"170\" rx=\"112\" ry=\"44\" fill=\"#d9d2b8\"/>\n    <!-- front quarter (shoulder) -->\n    <path d=\"M104 150 C 110 128, 150 124, 168 138 C 178 160, 170 196, 150 206 C 126 206, 104 190, 104 150 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n    <!-- hind quarter -->\n    <path d=\"M252 134 C 276 122, 312 130, 320 160 C 322 190, 300 206, 272 206 C 252 196, 240 160, 252 134 Z\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/>\n    <!-- backstrap strip along the spine -->\n    <path d=\"M122 132 C 160 118, 260 118, 310 134 L 310 146 C 260 130, 160 130, 122 144 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n    <!-- tenderloin (inside, dashed) -->\n    <path d=\"M232 152 C 250 150, 262 154, 268 162\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/>\n    <!-- ribs and flank -->\n    <g stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\">\n      <path d=\"M176 150 C 180 170, 180 190, 176 206\"/>\n      <path d=\"M192 150 C 196 170, 196 190, 192 208\"/>\n      <path d=\"M208 150 C 212 170, 212 190, 208 208\"/>\n      <path d=\"M224 150 C 228 170, 228 190, 224 206\"/>\n    </g>\n    <!-- neck -->\n    <path d=\"M116 158 L80 108 L104 96 L140 142 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n    <!-- head -->\n    <ellipse cx=\"80\" cy=\"100\" rx=\"30\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n    <path d=\"M96 88 L112 68 L106 92 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n    <path d=\"M90 86 L94 58 M94 70 L84 60 M94 64 L104 52\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n    <!-- tail -->\n    <path d=\"M320 154 L336 146 L332 162 Z\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  </g>\n\n  <!-- leader lines and labels -->\n  <g stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\">\n    <path d=\"M140 160 L60 200\"/>\n    <path d=\"M290 162 L350 230\"/>\n    <path d=\"M216 128 L216 70\"/>\n    <path d=\"M250 158 L300 117\"/>\n    <path d=\"M200 180 L200 300\"/>\n    <path d=\"M110 128 L40 60\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\">\n    <text x=\"10\" y=\"216\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Front quarter</text>\n    <text x=\"10\" y=\"234\" fill=\"#23261f\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-size=\"14\">shoulder and</text>\n    <text x=\"10\" y=\"252\" fill=\"#23261f\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-size=\"14\">shank</text>\n    <text x=\"303\" y=\"246\" fill=\"#6b4f35\">Hind quarter</text>\n    <text x=\"303\" y=\"264\" fill=\"#23261f\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-size=\"14\">the big roasts</text>\n    <text x=\"150\" y=\"60\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Backstrap (loin)</text>\n    <text x=\"150\" y=\"78\" fill=\"#23261f\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-size=\"14\">both sides of the spine</text>\n    <text x=\"392\" y=\"96\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"end\">Tenderloin</text>\n    <text x=\"392\" y=\"113\" fill=\"#23261f\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"end\">inside, under the spine</text>\n    <text x=\"150\" y=\"318\" fill=\"#6b4f35\">Ribs and flank</text>\n    <text x=\"150\" y=\"336\" fill=\"#23261f\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-size=\"14\">trim the meat off the bone</text>\n    <text x=\"10\" y=\"52\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Neck</text>\n  </g>\n\n  <!-- legend -->\n  <rect x=\"16\" y=\"360\" width=\"368\" height=\"116\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1ead8\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"28\" y=\"384\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">BC legal edible portions, big game:</text>\n  <text x=\"28\" y=\"406\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\">neck, ribs, four quarters and the loins.</text>\n  <text x=\"28\" y=\"428\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\">Take every one of these out. Leaving them is wastage.</text>\n  <text x=\"28\" y=\"448\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\">Heart and liver are optional extras.</text>\n  <text x=\"28\" y=\"466\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\">Take them if you like them.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Big game: neck, ribs, four quarters and loins come home <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Birds: both breasts <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. Bones, hide, head and guts can stay <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the law in full</summary><aside class=\"callout law\"><div class=\"callout-t\">The rule</div><p>Unlawful: \"To kill wildlife (with the exception of a fur bearing animal other than a black bear) and fail to remove from the carcass the edible portions (see definitions section) to the person's normal dwelling place or to a meat cutter or the owner or operator of a cold storage plant\" (95%, synopsis p. 12).</p></aside><ul><li><button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Edible portions\">Edible portions</button> for big game: \"the edible portions of the neck, ribs, four quarters and the loins of the animal\" (95%, p. 3).</li><li>Game birds: \"the edible portions of both breasts of the bird\" (95%, p. 3).</li><li>You may hand the animal to someone else who then takes the edible portions home. The duty moves with the meat (95%, p. 12).</li><li>Boning out is fine. Bones, hide, head and guts can stay at the site, or go to a landfill (95%, p. 12; p. 81 on landfill disposal of cervid parts).</li><li>Not within municipal boundaries and not where people go: a carcass is an attractant (95%, p. 9, p. 15).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"An all terrain vehicle with a cased rifle and the magazine removed. Chamber empty and magazine off before you touch the ATV. A round in the chamber or in an attached magazine counts as loaded.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">Rifle and ATV: unloaded, every time</text><g transform=\"translate(160 168)\"><circle cx=\"-60\" cy=\"40\" r=\"26\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"40\" r=\"26\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-60\" cy=\"40\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#9a9a8a\"/><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"40\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#9a9a8a\"/><path d=\"M-96 18 L-70 -4 L70 -4 L98 18 L90 30 L-90 30 Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><rect x=\"-14\" y=\"-16\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M-56 -4 L-50 -32 M-62 -32 L-38 -32\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><rect x=\"-100\" y=\"-12\" width=\"44\" height=\"8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><rect x=\"56\" y=\"-12\" width=\"44\" height=\"8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/></g><rect x=\"220\" y=\"62\" width=\"150\" height=\"24\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"295\" y=\"79\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\">cased rifle</text><rect x=\"250\" y=\"102\" width=\"26\" height=\"34\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#9a9a8a\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"286\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">magazine</text><text x=\"286\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">out</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2e7d32\">Chamber empty,</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2e7d32\">magazine off</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">before you touch the ATV</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#b3261e\">Loaded = round in the chamber</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#b3261e\">or in an attached magazine</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>ATV (all terrain vehicle): no live round in the chamber or attached magazine <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>No hunting from it. Check closures for your MU (Management Unit) <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Region 3: MUs 3-28, 3-29, 3-30 and part of 3-17 closed Sept 1 to Dec 10 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the Wildlife Act rules in full</summary><ul><li>An ATV is a \"motor vehicle\" under the hunting rules (95%, p. 4 definition).</li><li>Unlawful: a firearm \"containing live ammunition in its breech or in its magazine attached to the firearm, in or on a railway car, motor vehicle, sleigh, aircraft, bicycle or other conveyance\" (99%, page 11, item 28 (2 October 2026 edition)).</li><li>So: magazine out, chamber empty, before you touch the ATV. Clip with rounds in the rifle counts as loaded (95%, p. 3).</li><li>Unlawful \"To hunt wildlife from a motor vehicle\" (99%, page 11, item 22 (2 October 2026 edition)).</li><li>Motor Vehicle for Hunting Closed Area: using a motor vehicle \"to hunt, transport wildlife, transport equipment and supplies which are intended for or in support of hunting, or transport hunters to and from the location of wildlife is prohibited\" (95%, p. 10).</li><li>\"Unless specifically exempted, all motor vehicle prohibitions include private land\" (95%, p. 10).</li><li>Region 3 ATV for Hunting Closed Areas: \"from Sept 1 - Dec 10 in MUs 3-28, 3-29, 3-30, and that portion of MU 3-17 shown on Map C3\" (95%, p. 33).</li><li>Stake Lake cross country ski trails near Kamloops: closed to ATVs and snowmobiles (95%, p. 33).</li><li>Maps for every closure: <a href=\"https://www.gov.bc.ca/motorvehicleprohibitions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">gov.bc.ca/motorvehicleprohibitions</a> (95%, p. 10). Signs may be missing. \"The regulation is the final authority\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>You need</th><th>When</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Registration, plate shown</td><td>Always <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Helmet</td><td>Ride astride <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Driver's licence, $200,000 liability</td><td>On a Forest Service Road <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Spark arrestor</td><td>Wildfire conditions <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>ORV (Off Road Vehicle) fines: $230 unregistered, $368 careless <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the ORV Act in full</summary><ul><li>The <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"ORV\">ORV</button> (Off Road Vehicle) Act \"applies to ORVs on Crown land and prescribed private land\" (95%, p. 9).</li><li>\"Mandatory registration applies to ORVs. The plate or sticker must be clearly displayed on the front, back or left side of the ORV\" (95%, p. 9). Registration is through the Insurance Corporation of British Columbia (95%, ORV Act s. 4).</li><li>\"Mandatory safety laws apply to all ORVs; this includes helmets for ride astride ORVs and seatbelts (if installed). People under 16 must be supervised by an adult at least 19 years\" (95%, p. 9).</li><li>\"While travelling on a Forest Service Road, operators of ATVs are required to hold a valid driver's licence and carry a minimum of $200,000 third party liability insurance\" (95%, p. 9).</li><li>Carry government photo ID if you are 12 or older (95%, BC ORV page).</li><li>Fines: $230 for an unregistered ORV, $368 for careless operation (95%, BC ORV page).</li><li>Spark arrestor required during wildfire conditions. $460 ticket without one (95%, BC ORV page).</li><li>Crossing or riding a public highway needs ICBC basic insurance and a free police issued operation permit where it applies (90%, BC ORV page and search summary). <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> with ICBC for your route.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Game bags strapped on the front and rear racks of an all terrain vehicle, meat kept away from the exhaust. Drive slowly with no side hills. Take the rifle with you, never leave it on a parked quad.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">Meat on the ATV rack</text><g transform=\"translate(200 200)\"><circle cx=\"-60\" cy=\"40\" r=\"26\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"40\" r=\"26\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-60\" cy=\"40\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#9a9a8a\"/><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"40\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#9a9a8a\"/><path d=\"M-96 18 L-70 -4 L70 -4 L98 18 L90 30 L-90 30 Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><rect x=\"-14\" y=\"-16\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M-56 -4 L-50 -32 M-62 -32 L-38 -32\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><rect x=\"-100\" y=\"-12\" width=\"44\" height=\"8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><rect x=\"56\" y=\"-12\" width=\"44\" height=\"8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/></g><path d=\"M108 126 q 22.0 -8 44 0 l -3 50 q -19.0 7 -38 0 Z\" fill=\"#f4efe2\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M156 126 q 22.0 -8 44 0 l -3 50 q -19.0 7 -38 0 Z\" fill=\"#f4efe2\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M250 126 q 22.0 -8 44 0 l -3 50 q -19.0 7 -38 0 Z\" fill=\"#f4efe2\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M298 126 q 22.0 -8 44 0 l -3 50 q -19.0 7 -38 0 Z\" fill=\"#f4efe2\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M100 166 L350 166\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/><text x=\"225\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#e8590c\">straps over every bag</text><rect x=\"300\" y=\"222\" width=\"22\" height=\"8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#b3261e\">exhaust:</text><text x=\"318\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#b3261e\">meat away</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">Low speed. No side hills (Tip).</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">The rifle goes with you, not on a parked quad</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Rifle unloaded in transport. It goes with you, not on the parked quad (95%, Tip).</li><li>Licence travels with the meat. Brother's deer: his Record of Receipt <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: firearms and game in detail</summary><ul><li>Federal transport rule: a non restricted rifle may be transported only if \"it is unloaded\" (95%, SOR/98-209 s. 10).</li><li>Unattended ATV with the rifle on it: no lockable trunk, so the rifle must be \"not visible from outside the vehicle\" and the compartment \"securely locked\" (95%, s. 10). Practical answer: the rifle goes with you, not on the parked quad. Tip.</li><li>Carrying your own game on an ATV: no extra rule in the synopsis beyond closures (85%, my reading). The licence travels with the meat (95%, p. 15).</li><li>Carrying your brother's deer alone: his Record of Receipt in your pocket (95%, p. 15).</li><li>Strap quarters in game bags on the rear rack, meat away from the exhaust. Tip.</li><li>Whole deer across the front rack: head up, belly cavity open, drive slowly. Tip.</li><li>A loaded rack changes the handling. Low speed, no side hills. Tip.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation: a frame pack on a hunter. The heaviest piece, a quarter, goes in first, high and close to the back. Lighter bags go below it. Straps cinch everything tight. Carry 20 to 30 kilograms per trip.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">Pack it: heavy, high, tight to your back</text><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"70\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3.5\"/><path d=\"M120 84 L116 190\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M116 190 L104 280\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M116 190 L136 280\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"132\" y=\"74\" width=\"12\" height=\"190\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"132\" y=\"256\" width=\"70\" height=\"10\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"0.4s\" dur=\".3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"80 -60;0 0\" begin=\"0.4s\" dur=\".8s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"146\" y=\"90\" width=\"70\" height=\"70\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#e6b9a0\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"181.0\" y=\"130.0\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">quarter</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"1.6s\" dur=\".3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"80 -60;0 0\" begin=\"1.6s\" dur=\".8s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"146\" y=\"164\" width=\"62\" height=\"50\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#f4efe2\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"177.0\" y=\"194.0\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">bag</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"2.6s\" dur=\".3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"80 -60;0 0\" begin=\"2.6s\" dur=\".8s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"146\" y=\"218\" width=\"56\" height=\"36\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#f4efe2\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"174.0\" y=\"241.0\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">bag</text></g><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"222\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"4\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"3.8s\" dur=\"0.3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></line><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"214\" y2=\"176\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"4\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"4.1s\" dur=\"0.3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></line><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"232\" x2=\"214\" y2=\"232\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"4\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"4.3999999999999995s\" dur=\"0.3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></line><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"4.8s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"240\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Heaviest piece</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">high and close</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Straps tight</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"5.6s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"240\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">20 to 30 kg per</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"248\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">trip (Tip)</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Heavy piece high and close, then strap it tight. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>20 to 30 kg per trip is sustainable for a fit adult (Tip).</li><li>Going back to a cache: wind in your face, make noise <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: packs, sleds and drags</summary><ul><li>A pack frame with a load shelf carries a quarter or two bags. Strap the load high and tight to your back. Tip.</li><li>Fit adult, rough ground: 20 to 30 kg per trip is sustainable. 40 kg is a one trip hero load. Tip.</li><li>\"A load that blocks your view or pulls you off balance is too heavy\" (70%, BC Outdoors Magazine).</li><li>Sleds: a plastic game sled or kids toboggan on snow, with a rope harness. Whole deer in one pull downhill. Tip.</li><li>Drag a whole deer by the antlers or a rope around the neck, head first, hide on. Tip.</li><li>Return trips: approach the cache with the wind in your face and make noise. Bears claim meat (70%, BC Outdoors Magazine).</li></ul></details><a class=\"yt-card\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_gyYSHRjYKQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"yt-play\">▶</span><span class=\"yt-text\"><b>How to Pack Out Big Game | Brute Meat Loading Tutorial</b><small>Heavy meat high and close to your back.<br>Eberlestock, YouTube, 9 min. Needs internet.</small></span></a>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart of meat yield. Average deer: 49 kg field dressed gives 24 kg of boneless meat. Average buck: 59 kg gives 28 kg. Large bull moose: about 430 kg field dressed gives about 225 kg boneless. Deer yield is about 48 percent of field dressed weight.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">How much meat comes home</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Deer (scale 0 to 60 kg)</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"88\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#23261f\">Deer, avg</text><rect x=\"120\" y=\"64\" width=\"186.2\" height=\"18\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"120\" y=\"84\" width=\"91.19999999999999\" height=\"18\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"310.2\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">49 kg</text><text x=\"215.2\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">24 kg</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#23261f\">Buck, avg</text><rect x=\"120\" y=\"110\" width=\"224.2\" height=\"18\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"120\" y=\"130\" width=\"106.39999999999998\" height=\"18\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"348.2\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">59 kg</text><text x=\"230.39999999999998\" y=\"144\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">28 kg</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Bull moose (scale 0 to 450 kg)</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#23261f\">Large bull</text><rect x=\"120\" y=\"190\" width=\"249.39999999999998\" height=\"18\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"120\" y=\"210\" width=\"130.5\" height=\"18\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"365.4\" y=\"204\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#fff\">430 kg</text><text x=\"254.5\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">225 kg (65%)</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"250\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"42\" y=\"261\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#23261f\">field dressed</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"250\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"172\" y=\"261\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#23261f\">boneless meat</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Deer: about 48% of field dressed weight</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Deer: about 48% of field dressed weight is meat (70 to 80%).</li><li>Bone in quarters weigh about double the meat in them (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the full weight table</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Animal</th><th>Field dressed</th><th>Boneless meat</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>White tailed deer, average of 115</td><td>49 kg (108 lb)</td><td>24 kg (52 lb), about 48%</td><td>Ohio Department of Natural Resources, 2017 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></td></tr><tr><td>White tailed buck, average</td><td>59 kg (130 lb)</td><td>28 kg (63 lb)</td><td>Ohio Department of Natural Resources <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Deer, rule of thumb</td><td>100%</td><td>about 48% of field dressed weight, about 60% of a skinned carcass</td><td>National Deer Association <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Cow moose, live</td><td>340 to 420 kg</td><td>Not stated</td><td>BC synopsis definition <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Large bull moose, live about 725 kg (1,600 lb)</td><td>about 430 kg (950 lb)</td><td>about 225 kg (500 lb)</td><td>Alaska Department of Fish and Game, search summary <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Elk, field dressed</td><td>80 to 245 kg (176 to 540 lb)</td><td>40 to 120 kg (88 to 270 lb)</td><td>University of Wyoming via secondary summary <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Black bear</td><td><span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span></td><td><span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span></td><td>No source confirmed</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Mule deer bucks in Region 3 run bigger than the Ohio white tails. Expect 25 to 35 kg of boneless meat from a mature buck (Tip, estimate).</li><li>Bone in quarters weigh roughly double the boneless meat in them (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"One moose packed by two people: two hind quarters of about 45 to 55 kg each, two front quarters of about 35 to 40 kg each, and bags of loins, neck, rib meat and trim, plus antlers and gear. About 7 loads at 30 kg each, 4 trips each, a full day for 1 kilometre. A tip, not a measured figure.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">One moose, two people: count the trips</text><path d=\"M36 54 q 23.0 -8 46 0 l -3 56 q -20.0 7 -40 0 Z\" fill=\"#e6b9a0\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"58\" y=\"88\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">Hind</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">45 to 55 kg</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"146\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#e8590c\">split in 2</text><path d=\"M132 54 q 23.0 -8 46 0 l -3 56 q -20.0 7 -40 0 Z\" fill=\"#e6b9a0\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"154\" y=\"88\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">Hind</text><text x=\"154\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">45 to 55 kg</text><text x=\"154\" y=\"146\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#e8590c\">split in 2</text><path d=\"M228 54 q 23.0 -8 46 0 l -3 56 q -20.0 7 -40 0 Z\" fill=\"#e6b9a0\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"250\" y=\"88\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">Front</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">35 to 40 kg</text><path d=\"M324 54 q 23.0 -8 46 0 l -3 56 q -20.0 7 -40 0 Z\" fill=\"#e6b9a0\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"346\" y=\"88\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">Front</text><text x=\"346\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">35 to 40 kg</text><path d=\"M36 158 q 23.0 -8 46 0 l -3 56 q -20.0 7 -40 0 Z\" fill=\"#f4efe2\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"58\" y=\"192\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">Bags</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">loins, neck</text><path d=\"M132 158 q 23.0 -8 46 0 l -3 56 q -20.0 7 -40 0 Z\" fill=\"#f4efe2\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"154\" y=\"192\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">Bags</text><text x=\"154\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">ribs, trim</text><path d=\"M228 158 q 23.0 -8 46 0 l -3 56 q -20.0 7 -40 0 Z\" fill=\"#f4efe2\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"250\" y=\"192\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">Bags</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">trim</text><path d=\"M324 188 q 22 -30 44 0 M330 178 l -8 -14 M346 166 l 0 -16 M362 178 l 8 -14\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"5\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"346\" y=\"212\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">Antlers</text><text x=\"346\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">and gear</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">About 7 loads at 30 kg each: 4 trips each,</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">plus antlers. A full day for 1 km (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>One deer, two people, 1 km: one trip each (Tip).</li><li>Never shoot a moose farther than four return trips before dark (Tip).</li><li>A bone in hind quarter (45 to 55 kg) is heavier than a 30 kg load: bone it out or cut it in two before you lift it (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the trip math in detail</summary><ul><li>One deer, two people, 1 km in. Boneless meat about 25 kg, plus head and cape if wanted. One trip each (Tip).</li><li>Same deer whole and gutted: about 50 kg. One hard drag, or an ATV if the area allows (Tip).</li><li>One moose, two people, no ATV. Say 200 kg boneless plus antlers (Tip, from the table above).<ul><li>Bone in quarters: hind about 45 to 55 kg each, front about 35 to 40 kg each. Plus 40 to 50 kg of loins, neck, rib and trim in bags (Tip).</li><li>At 30 kg per person per trip: about 7 loads, so 4 trips each, plus one for antlers and gear. A full day for 1 km, two days for 3 km (Tip).</li><li>A bone in hind quarter is over 30 kg, so it never goes in one load: bone it out, or saw it into two pieces. Your safe load is the one you can carry on rough ground without falling; 30 kg is a starting point, not a rule (Tip, 70%).</li><li>Boned out: about 7 loads still, lighter each but more bags. The bones are the saving on a long pack (Tip).</li></ul></li><li>Rule of thumb: never shoot a moose further from the ATV or truck than you can make four return trips before dark. Tip.</li></ul><aside class=\"callout lean\"><div class=\"callout-t\">My lean (opinion)</div><p>Deer first year: whole, gutted, dragged or on the ATV rack. Moose later: gutless, boned out, frame packs, and a drop point where the ATV can legally reach.</p></aside></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>ATV into a closed area \"to pick up the deer\"</td><td>Pack it out on foot</td></tr><tr><td>Magazine in the rifle on the rack</td><td>That is loaded: take it out</td></tr><tr><td>One giant load</td><td>20 to 30 kg trips</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>The animal is yours when the last bag is in the truck, not when it hits the ground.</p></aside><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: 3 common mistakes and the field habit</summary><ul><li>Riding the ATV into an ATV for Hunting Closed Area \"just to pick up the deer\".</li><li>Rifle on the rack with the magazine in. That is loaded in BC.</li><li>One giant load that ends in a fall, a torn knee and meat still on the hill.</li></ul><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Before the shot: where is the ATV allowed, how far is the drop point, how many trips, how much light.</p></aside></details>","<div class=\"checklist\" data-list=\"p5s9-pack\"><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"p5s9-pack:0\"><span>ATV closure map checked for this MU</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"p5s9-pack:1\"><span>ATV registered, plate shown, helmet on</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"p5s9-pack:2\"><span>Driver's licence and $200,000 liability insurance for the FSR</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"p5s9-pack:3\"><span>Magazine out and chamber empty before the ATV</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"p5s9-pack:4\"><span>Spark arrestor if fire season</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"p5s9-pack:5\"><span>Trips counted, light counted</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"p5s9-pack:6\"><span>Every edible portion bagged and out</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"p5s9-pack:7\"><span>Licence with the meat, Record of Receipt if needed</span></label></div>","<ul><li>Synopsis, ORV (Off Road Vehicle) Act, BC ORV pages and federal transport rules 95%. Yields 60 to 80%. Checked 2026-10-01.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: all sources</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/assets/gov/sports-recreation-arts-and-culture/outdoor-recreation/fishing-and-hunting/hunting/regulations/hunting-trapping-synopsis.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028</a>, read directly. Printed p. 3 (loaded, edible portions), p. 4 (motor vehicle), p. 9 (ORV Act, FSR insurance, carcasses), p. 10 (motor vehicle prohibitions), p. 11 (22, 27), p. 12 (44), p. 15 (transport, attractants), p. 33 (Region 3 closures). Checked 2026-10-01. Quotes have hyphens removed.</li><li><a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/gov/content/industry/crown-land-water/crown-land/crown-land-uses/off-road-vehicles\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Off road vehicles page</a> and <a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/gov/content/industry/crown-land-water/crown-land/crown-land-uses/off-road-vehicles/safety\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ORV safety page</a>, read directly. Checked 2026-10-01.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.bclaws.gov.bc.ca/civix/document/id/complete/statreg/14005\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Off Road Vehicle Act, SBC 2014 c. 14</a>, read directly, s. 4. Checked 2026-10-01.</li><li><a href=\"https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/regulations/SOR-98-209/FullText.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Storage, Display, Transportation and Handling of Firearms by Individuals Regulations, SOR/98-209, s. 10</a>, read directly. Checked 2026-10-01.</li><li><a href=\"https://dam.assets.ohio.gov/image/upload/ohiodnr.gov/documents/wildlife/wild-ohio-harvest-community/Venison%20Yield.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ohio Department of Natural Resources, Venison meat yield (PDF)</a>, read directly, 80%. <a href=\"https://deerassociation.com/how-much-venison-can-you-expect-from-your-deer/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">National Deer Association, how much venison</a>, 70%. Checked 2026-10-01.</li><li>Moose and elk yields: search summaries only, 60 to 65%. <a href=\"https://www.adfg.alaska.gov/index.cfm?adfg=moosehunting.main\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Alaska Department of Fish and Game moose hunting page</a> did not show the figures when read. <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.bcoutdoorsmagazine.com/after-the-shot/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Outdoors Magazine, After the shot</a>, 70%. Trip math and load limits: Tip.</li></ul></details>"]